: "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_016nJkEWKmobU3hBPViishCc", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 53220, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_016nJkEWKmobU3hBPViishCc", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 54661, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01Tn4RBtYnHFdC92xAS3kxzm", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 54961, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01Tn4RBtYnHFdC92xAS3kxzm", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 54961, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01Tn4RBtYnHFdC92xAS3kxzm", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 59646, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "checkout-api is back on v2.3.0 in all regions and healthy again. I opened the SEV2 incident, **INC-0001**.\n\n1. **Rollback target:** v2.3.0 is the newest release marked healthy in the deploy history. The broken deploy was v2.3.1, which was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west with an 18% error rate. Its release candidate, v2.3.1-rc, was also unhealthy.\n2. **Rollback:** The first attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error. For a while, us-east ran v2.3.0 while us-west and eu-west stayed on v2.3.1. I retried, and it finished in all three regions. All regions now run v2.3.0, and the error rate is down to 0.2%.\n3. **Incident:** The request to create the incident timed out. Before retrying, I checked the incident list and saw it had been created, so there's no duplicate. It describes the failure, the rollback (including the partial first attempt) and the recovery. It also lists two follow-ups: find why v2.3.1 failed, and look into the orchestrator error.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_0185GjTzUiexHgCb9YRjMcYL", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01JCUqc5vyBncaVxsdRsoLBT", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01EktcfauV9J97SUZqFfJSh7", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_0159vSzQ8fdTAyNoWvja89ha", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_0156M7Edba1ZJ7zrE6EJ6Esn", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01RWv1wZzFESLQdj9G5h11Nr", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_0195seyx7x89me8FUMfqBSU4", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_016nJkEWKmobU3hBPViishCc", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks - rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the latest deploy (v2.3.1), checkout-api failed health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an 18% error rate. The latest release marked healthy in deploy history was v2.3.0; v2.3.1-rc and v2.3.1 were both unhealthy. The SRE agent rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0. The first rollback stopped after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1 for a while. A second rollback finished in all regions. All regions now run v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, and look into the rollback orchestrator error.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01Tn4RBtYnHFdC92xAS3kxzm", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is back on v2.3.0 in all regions and healthy again. I opened the SEV2 incident, **INC-0001**.\n\n1. **Rollback target:** v2.3.0 is the newest release marked healthy in the deploy history. The broken deploy was v2.3.1, which was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west with an 18% error rate. Its release candidate, v2.3.1-rc, was also unhealthy.\n2. **Rollback:** The first attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error. For a while, us-east ran v2.3.0 while us-west and eu-west stayed on v2.3.1. I retried, and it finished in all three regions. All regions now run v2.3.0, and the error rate is down to 0.2%.\n3. **Incident:** The request to create the incident timed out. Before retrying, I checked the incident list and saw it had been created, so there's no duplicate. It describes the failure, the rollback (including the partial first attempt) and the recovery. It also lists two follow-ups: find why v2.3.1 failed, and look into the orchestrator error.", "type": "text"}]}]}